stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> DECLARED: FP1 node declared in the graph with loop members, max iterations and tolerance
    DECLARED --> SEEDED: FP2 starting iterate taken from the declared seed rule
    SEEDED --> ITERATING: FP3 first pass evaluates every loop member against the pinned rule versions
    ITERATING --> ITERATING: FP4 delta above tolerance and iteration count below the limit
    ITERATING --> CONVERGED: FP5 delta at or under tolerance
    ITERATING --> OSCILLATING: FP6 the same iterate pair repeats
    ITERATING --> LIMIT_REACHED: FP7 iteration count reaches max iterations
    OSCILLATING --> LIMIT_REACHED: FP8 no tie-break rule declared for this node
    CONVERGED --> ROUNDED: FP9 statutory rounding applied once to the converged values only
    ROUNDED --> [*]: FP10 result published with iterate history in the computation trace
    LIMIT_REACHED --> BLOCKED: FP11 run stops at PROCESSED, names node, employee and last two iterates
    BLOCKED --> [*]: FP12 no intermediate iterate is ever published

    note right of ITERATING
      Rule versions are pinned before the loop
      and are never re-resolved mid-loop, so
      replay reproduces the iterate sequence.
    end note

    note right of BLOCKED
      Blocking is the correct outcome. A published
      first iterate under-accrues gratuity and
      breaks the CTC reconciliation.
    end note
